        "content": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>I want to define a class where one of the fields is an instance of a class so the synthesizer can look for it later. The problem I have is that currently I need to add the <code>[instance]</code> attribute right after I declared my class.  I would like to know if it is possible to add this attribute during the class declaration.</p>\n<p>Here is a mwe.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ty_ne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ty</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ty</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- failed to synthesize Nonempty test.ty</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">--need to add this manually</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ty_ne</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- test.ty_ne</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there a way to do this? Thanks in advance :)</p>",
        "id": 619271971,
        "sender_full_name": "Ivan Martinez Comas",
        "timestamp": 1787747602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>AFAIK, this is not possible in current Lean 4. Attributes cannot yet be attached directly to structure/class fields. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13382\">Lean PR #13382 proposes support for field attributes.</a></p>",
        "id": 619283336,
        "sender_full_name": "Colin Bundschu",
        "timestamp": 1787750549
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see,  many thanks!</p>",
